{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>If it be so.</b> If the matter is so as you said — that the man dealt harshly with you, yet he is one who fears Elohim:" "<b>Then.</b> Of necessity it is fitting that <b>this</b> you do:" "<b>Take of the choice fruits of the land in your vessels a little balm.</b> For indeed a gift brought to a man panicked for money must be great in quantity so as to satisfy the eye, and of this kind was Jacob's gift to Esau. But when it is brought to a noble who does not count silver, it should be small — but a thing chosen from things found only in small measure, and that in royal palaces; and of this kind was this gift to Joseph." "<b>And bring down to the man a gift.</b> Before you go to see his face, so that you may see how he receives the gift with favor. And by this you will know how he will receive you with a cheerful countenance, as it says (Judges 13:23): לוּ חָפֵץ ה' לַהֲמִיתֵנוּ לֹא לָקַח מִיָּדֵנוּ עוֹלָה וּמִנְחָה. And afterward:"], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:26.258698800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}